WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.263
Is Priya’s bakery a small employer?

00:00:02.263 --> 00:00:06.412
Maryland defines a small employer as one that employed an average

00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:10.562
of not more than 50 employees during the preceding calendar year.

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:15.842
The count is full-time employees, those averaging 30 or more hours a week, plus

00:00:15.842 --> 00:00:21.123
full-time equivalents, calculated each month by dividing the hours of part-time employees by 120.

00:00:21.123 --> 00:00:22.632
Seasonal workers are excluded.

00:00:22.632 --> 00:00:27.158
Priya has 14 full-time workers and six part-timers at 20 hours a

00:00:27.158 --> 00:00:31.685
week, about 480 part-time hours a month, which is four full-time equivalents.

00:00:31.685 --> 00:00:33.948
Eighteen in all: a small employer.

00:00:33.948 --> 00:00:37.720
A firm with 60 full-time workers is a large group.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.510
A carrier that sells small group coverage in Maryland must accept every

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:47.299
small employer that applies and meets its uniformly applied participation and contribution

00:00:47.299 --> 00:00:52.089
requirements, and must enroll every eligible employee the employer offers coverage to.

00:00:52.089 --> 00:00:56.479
It may not deny, limit or condition coverage because of the

00:00:56.479 --> 00:01:00.869
health status of the employer’s workers, and discriminating against employees on

00:01:00.869 --> 00:01:04.861
the basis of health status is an unfair trade practice.

00:01:04.861 --> 00:01:09.650
The only lawful reasons to turn down a small group are failure

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:14.440
to meet participation or contribution rules, location outside the carrier’s service area

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.830
or the carrier’s lack of capacity, applied to all groups alike.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:23.448
Carriers must give small employers plain-language disclosure of the plan’s

00:01:23.448 --> 00:01:28.066
benefits, exclusions, premium rating practices, renewability terms and participation requirements

00:01:28.066 --> 00:01:32.223
before the sale, so Priya can compare offers honestly.

00:01:32.223 --> 00:01:38.226
Eligible employees are those the employer offers coverage to; the employer may limit

00:01:38.226 --> 00:01:44.230
eligibility to full-time employees or include part-time employees working at least 17.5 hours

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:49.772
a week, but it must apply the choice to the whole class.

00:01:49.772 --> 00:01:53.928
Dependents are eligible under the rules in Lesson 37.

00:01:53.928 --> 00:01:57.161
Waiting periods may not exceed 90 days.

00:01:57.161 --> 00:02:00.855
An employee who declines may join later only

00:02:00.855 --> 00:02:04.550
at open enrollment or a special enrollment event.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.301
Small group premiums are set by modified community rating.

00:02:08.301 --> 00:02:13.718
For plans issued or renewed since 2014, rates may vary only by whether

00:02:13.718 --> 00:02:19.136
coverage is individual or family, by rating area, by age within a 3

00:02:19.136 --> 00:02:24.553
to 1 ratio for adults, and by tobacco use within 1.5 to 1.

00:02:24.553 --> 00:02:28.720
Nothing else: not health, not claims, not industry, not gender.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.888
Rates are fixed for the entire plan year, so Priya’s

00:02:32.888 --> 00:02:36.638
premium cannot change midyear when an employee gets sick.

00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:41.222
Carriers must use accepted actuarial methods and apply risk adjustment consistently.

00:02:41.222 --> 00:02:46.640
Grandfathered small group plans keep an older Maryland rating structure with limited adjustments.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.401
Small group coverage is guaranteed renewable at the employer’s option.

00:02:50.401 --> 00:02:55.291
A carrier may refuse to renew only for nonpayment of premium, fraud or

00:02:55.291 --> 00:03:00.180
intentional misrepresentation, failure to meet participation or contribution requirements, the employer leaving the

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:05.070
carrier’s service area, or the carrier’s withdrawal from the small group market with

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:09.583
the required notice, after which it may not reenter for five years.

00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:12.969
The group’s claims, the illness of an employee or

00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:15.978
the age of the workforce are never grounds.

00:03:15.978 --> 00:03:18.987
Renewal premiums may change within the rating rules.

00:03:18.987 --> 00:03:23.500
This is HIPAA’s renewability guarantee as implemented in Maryland’s small group law.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:29.620
As a small employer, Priya may buy directly from a carrier or through Maryland

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:35.739
Health Connection for Small Business, the SHOP marketplace, with Theo as her authorized producer.

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:40.547
Either way she gets guaranteed availability, community rating and guaranteed renewability.

00:03:40.547 --> 00:03:45.793
Through SHOP she may qualify for the small business health care tax

00:03:45.793 --> 00:03:51.038
credit if she has fewer than 25 full-time equivalent employees and modest

00:03:51.038 --> 00:03:55.409
average wages, and she can offer employee choice among plans.

00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:59.343
She must meet the carrier’s participation and contribution rules

00:03:59.343 --> 00:04:02.840
and may define eligibility for her part-time staff.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.900
Her employees’ health never enters the price.
